   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Royal Australasian College of Surgeons (RACS) Global Health program deploys volunteer surgical teams to Pacific nations, including the Federated States of Micronesia. In 2024, an ear, nose and throat focused visit to Pohnpei (27 Sept&#x2013;5 Oct) included a surgeon, anesthetist, audiologist, and perioperative nurse. The team conducted 97 consultations (81 adults, 16 pediatric), with common presentations of deafness, ear perforations, and rhinitis. Procedures performed included myringoplasties, examination under anaesthetic for ears/grommets, and nasal polypectomies. Pohnpei State health staff and students actively supported clinical and theatre activities, gaining skills and confidence throughout the week.
&#x200d;
The most recent visit to Chuuk (27 Mar&#x2013;6 Apr 2025) focused on urological care, with a team comprising a surgeon, anesthetist, clinical nurse specialist, and occupational therapy (OT) nurse. Presentations included female continence issues, often among multigravida women with no prior pelvic floor therapy, and male lower urinary tract symptoms. Bladder outlet surgery was the main procedure performed. Chuuk State health staff including two local surgeons, an anesthetic scientific officer, and OT nurses were highly engaged and eager to learn. While language barriers were noted, collaboration and capacity building were strong across both locations.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
